Third-party notices
===================

MaKlipper does not copy, fork, or redistribute upstream source code. At
install time it clones the following projects, unmodified, from their
official repositories; they remain under their own licenses:

- Klipper (https://github.com/Klipper3d/klipper) — GPLv3
- Moonraker (https://github.com/Arksine/moonraker) — GPLv3
- Mainsail (https://github.com/meteyou/mainsail) — GPLv3
- Fluidd (https://github.com/fluidd-core/fluidd) — GPLv3

Runtime dependencies installed by the user or package managers (e.g.
libsodium — ISC license — via Homebrew; CPython — PSF license) are not
bundled by MaKlipper.

The two compatibility headers under maklipper/compat/include/ are original
small files (about 20-40 lines each) authored for this project. Their struct
layouts and constant values mirror the published Linux kernel UAPI
definitions (uapi/linux/can.h, uapi/linux/prctl.h), which are factual
interfaces rather than protectable expression; they were not copied from
kernel sources.
